# Day 006 – Hero Reset

## Date

04 August 2026

---

## What I Did Today

Today was basically a fresh start for the Hero section.

I kept trying to fix the old layout, but every small change ended up creating another problem somewhere else. After going back and forth for quite a while, I finally decided to delete the entire Hero folder and rebuild everything from scratch.

Honestly, it feels much cleaner this way.

Instead of fighting old code, I'm now building a proper foundation from the beginning.

---

## Hero

Today wasn't really about writing lots of code.

It was about figuring out how I actually want the website to feel.

After spending a lot of time comparing my Procreate design with the website, I finally have a clear vision of how the Hero should work.

The landing page should start with only the main Hero content visible.

As the user scrolls, the Hero content will smoothly shrink and move to the left while the product showcase slides in from the right.

Once that layout is finished, I'll start working on the dashboard, floating badges, card rotation, and the final animations.

For now, I'm focusing on getting the layout right before adding any interactions.

I've decided to follow one simple rule throughout this project:

> First make it work. Then make it beautiful. Then make it reusable.

